AltoLeverageSwapperMultiTarget::setValidSwapTarget(address,bool)
├── given caller is not owner even when target is zero
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount before target validation and preserve target permissions
└── given caller is owner
    ├── when target is zero with either requested status
    │   └── it should revert with AltoLeverageSwapperInvalidInput and keep zero invalid
    ├── when requested status equals the current false or true status
    │   └── it should revert with AltoLeverageSwapperInvalidInput and preserve target permissions
    └── when target is nonzero and status changes
        ├── when target is an EOA
        │   └── it should allow adding and removing it without code validation
        ├── when target is a contract
        │   └── it should allow revoking and restoring its permission
        ├── when the caller is already whitelisted
        │   └── it should keep the caller whitelisted while adding and revoking target permissions
        ├── it should preserve owner the caller whitelist and the invalid zero target
        └── it should emit exactly one SetValidSwapTarget with the indexed target and requested status
